title: The Reichsexekution
subtitle: The Reichswehr marches into Dresden to remove the Saxon government.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 1923 and month >= 10 and month <= 11 and e23_reich_done = 0 and crisis = 0 and (e23_saxony_decided = 1 or e23_october_done = 1) and german_october != 3 and e23_red_region != 1
max-visits: 1
priority: 2
on-arrival: {!
if (!RG.e22) { this._runActions(this.game.scenes.e22_lib.onArrival); }
RG.district('saxony', {repression: 15});
RG.district('thuringia', {repression: 8});
RG.news('Reichswehr deposes the Saxon government', 3);
Q.e23_reich_done = 1;
Q.e23_had_ministers = Q.saxony_government == 1 ? 1 : 0;
Q.saxony_government = 0;
Q.spd_in_government = 0;
Q.government_name = 'Stresemann cabinet (DVP, Centre, DDP)';
!}

= The Reichsexekution

On 29 October a lieutenant and a squad of soldiers walk into the State Chancellery in Dresden and tell Erich Zeigner that he is no longer Minister-President. A Reich commissioner moves into his office the same afternoon. [? if e23_had_ministers = 1 : Our two ministers are escorted out of the building behind him. ?]

[? if bavaria_soviet != 2 : Kahr's Bavaria has defied Berlin for a month and received letters. Saxony has received three divisions. ?][? if bavaria_soviet = 2 : The Reich sends its army into Saxony because it does not dare to send it into Red Bavaria. ?] The Social Democrats leave Stresemann's cabinet in protest, and do nothing else.

[? if e23_october_done = 1 and german_october = 2 : The party has already had its October, and the Saxon workers know what it cost. ?][? if e23_october_done = 1 and german_october < 2 : The party called off its October, and the Saxon workers have not forgotten it. ?][? if e23_october_done = 0 : The Saxon workers are waiting to hear from the party. Some of them still have rifles. ?]

- @defend: Call the hundreds out to defend Saxony.
- @protest: Call a one-day protest strike.
- @yield: Protest in the press and the Landtag.

@defend
subtitle: [? if lock_uprising = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] The Reichswehr is already inside the fortress.
view-if: e23_october_done = 0
choose-if: lock_uprising < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids an armed rising.
on-arrival: {!
RG.e22.against('uprising');
Q.e23_october_path = 4;
RG.e22.octRise(['saxony', 'thuringia'], 'The Defence of Saxony', 'Hold Saxony and Thuringia until the Reichswehr gives up.', -2);
RG.district('saxony', {militancy: 10});
Q.lean_offensive += 3;
!}

The sirens in Chemnitz go at noon. The hundreds take the main station and the post office while the soldiers are still in their billets.

@protest
subtitle: Saxony's workers say no for a day. The army takes their names.
on-arrival: {!
RG.startStrike('saxony', true);
RG.endStrike('saxony', 'crushed');
RG.news('Soldiers fire on strikers in Freiberg', 2);
RG.ledger('Soldiers fired on our protest strike in Freiberg.', 'e23_freiberg');
if (!Q.e23_october_done) { Q.german_october = 0; Q.e23_october_done = 1; }
Q.worker_support += 2;
Q.spd_relation += 3;
!}

For a day the Saxon works stand still. In Freiberg soldiers fire into a crowd of strikers in the market square and kill twenty-three. The next morning the works open again.

@yield
subtitle: Nobody is killed. The Left will call it capitulation.
on-arrival: {!
RG.district('saxony', {loyalty: -6, militancy: -5});
if (!Q.e23_october_done) { Q.german_october = 0; Q.e23_october_done = 1; }
Q.offensive_satisfaction -= 8;
Q.unity -= 2;
!}

Our deputies walk out of the Landtag. The party holds protest meetings in the halls that the army has not closed yet.
